       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual maximum acetaminophen dose for an adult of 4,000 mg/day. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A dose like that risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function. A single 3,000 mg dose also exceeds the typical maximum of 1,000 mg per dose.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours**, or four times daily if your institution allows up to 4,000 mg/day\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add it as a note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
