       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a potentially toxic dose, and I don't know of any indication where it would be appropriate for an adult with normal liver function. The risk is acute liver injury, and I don't want to put that order into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO every 8 hours (3,000 mg/day), or 1000 mg PO four times daily if your institution allows up to 4,000 mg/day.\n- **Help you check the intent.** If you're trying to achieve a particular goal, such as fever or pain control, I can help you find a regimen that gets there. Adding a scheduled NSAID or another adjunct is one option.\n- **Suggest a pharmacy or attending review.** If you think there's a reason for an unusual dose, they can review it directly. If they approve it, they can enter it or tell you how to proceed.\n\nWhich standard dose would you like me to enter?"
      }
